[sai-00179] helpful=1 harmful=0 :: When a prompt requires hyperlinks, always use descriptive anchor text (e.g., '[Restaurant Name Official Website]') rather than raw URLs. If a prompt requires research (e.g., video links), perform actual searches. Never use placeholder URLs (e.g., 'a_b_c_d_e') or hallucinated links; if no real link is found, explicitly state 'No verified video content found' rather than providing a fake link.
[sai-00180] helpful=1 harmful=0 :: When a prompt provides a specific field order (e.g., Name -> Image -> Location -> Business Hours -> Website -> Bio), treat this sequence as a hard structural constraint. Before drafting, create a 'Field-Order Checklist' to ensure every item is placed in the exact sequence requested. Failure to follow the specified order is a critical rubric violation.
[sai-00184] helpful=2 harmful=0 :: When tasked with creating a structured form or questionnaire based on a rubric or reference document, perform a 'Rubric-to-Field' mapping before drafting. Create a table that lists every required field, sub-question, and structural element (e.g., checkboxes, blank lines, specific headers) mandated by the source. Do not begin drafting until this mapping is complete, and perform a final 'Compliance Audit' to verify that every rubric-mandated item is present and correctly formatted for the end-user to fill out.
