[sai-00232] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When generating compliance-driven documentation, treat every rubric criterion as a mandatory functional requirement rather than an opportunity for procedural abstraction or generic summaries. Before drafting, create a 'Requirement-to-Section' mapping table to ensure all technical data, metrics, and editorial guidelines are addressed; do not finalize the output until a 'Compliance Audit' confirms that 100% of these granular constraints are met with the necessary technical depth and evidence-based detail.
[sai-00233] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: For reports requiring district-level or stakeholder-specific analysis, perform a 'Granular Data-to-Section' mapping. Before drafting, create a checklist of all required entities (e.g., all four districts) and verify that each entity has a dedicated, data-rich section in the final output. Do not aggregate data into a single summary until all entity-specific requirements have been explicitly addressed and documented.
